---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - ALtoy" {base}>
    <main class="privacy-page">
        <h1>ALtoy Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated"><em>Last updated: 2026-04-23</em></p>

        <h2>What ALtoy is</h2>
        <p>ALtoy (<code>jforplay.github.io/altoy</code>) is a non-profit fan-made web viewer for Azur Lane KR game assets. It is a static website hosted on GitHub Pages with no server, no user accounts, and no database.</p>

        <h2>What data ALtoy collects from you</h2>
        <p>ALtoy does not collect personal information. The site stores the following only in your browser's local storage, on your device:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>UI preferences (theme, view mode, last active tab)</li>
            <li>Progress data you voluntarily enter (ship tracker, skin collection, island planner, etc.)</li>
            <li>Cached game data for performance (no personal data)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This data never leaves your device unless you explicitly enable Google Drive sync.</p>

        <h2>Google Drive sync (optional)</h2>
        <p>If you enable Google Drive sync, ALtoy uses the <code>drive.appdata</code> OAuth scope to store a single JSON file (<code>altoy-sync.json</code>) in a hidden, application-specific folder in your own Google Drive. This folder is invisible to other apps and not shown in your Drive's regular file list.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The file contains only the progress data listed above.</li>
            <li>Data is sent directly from your browser to Google's servers over HTTPS. ALtoy's developer never sees or stores this data.</li>
            <li>You can revoke ALtoy's access at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener noreferrer">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. You can also delete the file manually via Google Drive's "Manage apps" settings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>ALtoy uses Cloudflare Web Analytics for aggregate, privacy-preserving visitor statistics. Cloudflare Web Analytics does not use cookies and does not track individual users across sites.</p>

        <h2>Third-party resources</h2>
        <p>Pages load the following from external sources:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Google Fonts (for typography)</li>
            <li>Font Awesome via cdnjs.cloudflare.com (for icons)</li>
            <li>Fuse.js via cdn.jsdelivr.net (for search)</li>
            <li>Game assets (images, audio) from public GitHub-hosted repositories</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These services may receive your IP address and user-agent as part of normal web requests, per their own privacy policies.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>This is a non-commercial fan project. For questions, open an issue at the project's GitHub repository.</p>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
    /* Body styling only applies when /privacy/ is rendered (this file is the
       only one that loads this CSS). Gives the page a theme-aware background
       so dark mode doesn't leave dark text on a white canvas.

       Target html AND body with explicit background-color (not shorthand) so
       the rule is robust against whatever cascades in on other pages. */
    html,
    body {
        background-color: var(--bg-gradient-start);
        min-height: 100vh;
        margin: 0;
    }
    body {
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }
</style>

<style>
    .privacy-page {
        max-width: 720px;
        margin: 2rem auto;
        padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }
    .privacy-page h1 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }
    .privacy-page h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    }
    .privacy-page .updated {
        margin-top: 0;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .privacy-page p {
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }
    .privacy-page code {
        background: var(--bg-secondary);
        color: var(--text-primary);
        padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
        border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
        font-size: 0.9em;
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    }
    .privacy-page a {
        color: var(--accent-blue);
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .privacy-page a:hover {
        filter: brightness(1.15);
    }
    .privacy-page ul {
        padding-left: 1.5rem;
        margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
    }
    .privacy-page li {
        margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
        color: var(--text-primary);
    }
</style>
